# T11 known exceptions: rule <TAB> file <TAB> key <TAB> reason [<TAB> phase]
# key '*' exempts a whole file for that rule.  A KNOWN hit is reported, never failed.
# R1: the handoff/exit IMPLEMENTATIONS (separate TUs, reached only through the wrapped
# handoff_run; x2 §1).  They are the thing fe_priv.h's wrapper calls, not its callers.
R1	psp/usb_handoff.c	*	handoff_run's own implementation (ADR-0053); reached only via the hijacked handoff_run
R1	psp/lab_harness.c	*	lab build's lab_finish / ownership loss (x2 E3); reached via LAB_HANDOFF
# (R4: both fe_evt-argument calls T11 knew of -- r6-B3's sceCtrlSetSamplingCycle and
# sleep_sim's fe_host_sram_test_kill_handle -- were moved out of the EVT in HW-2.)
# R7 (tier C, C2-1): the frame loop's one harness read stays raw in every build: a player build folds
# HARNESS_INT, and a folded read would take the block out of its frame loop (frame parity, 2026-11-17).
R7	psp/fe/loop.inc.c	rewind_gedump	the only harness read inside the frame loop (static-once); raw so release and Lab compile the same frame loop (frame parity)
# R9 (rescore 2026-11-17): the rule's own description and self-test quote the phrases it forbids.
R9	tools/refactor/ci_greps.sh	*	R9's own description quotes the phrases
R9	tools/refactor/tests/abi-exit-ci_test_ci_greps.sh	*	the R9 mutants' descriptions quote the phrases
